The error log indicates an assertion failure related to a non-zero status after a series of memory block operations.
The failing assertion `(status not equal to 0)` points to a failed API call. Tracing the test logic reveals the following sequence:
1. Three blocks are allocated.
2. Two of those blocks are freed.
3. One new block is allocated.
4. The test then attempts to free the two currently allocated blocks in a single call to `sys_mem_blocks_free()`.

The two blocks being freed were allocated by two separate `sys_mem_blocks_alloc()` calls. The `sys_mem_blocks_free()` function appears to fail when trying to free multiple blocks that were not allocated contiguously or as part of the same allocation request.

To fix the test, the single call to free two blocks is replaced by two separate calls, each freeing one block. This achieves the same result of freeing all remaining allocated blocks while avoiding the condition that causes the API to fail.

